      "id": 9116,
      "finding_type": "financial",
      "summary": "Mordashov investment vehicle that channeled sanctioned oligarch capital into US tech companies including Centice",
      "detail": "S-Group Capital Management, founded 2007 in Moscow, manages financial assets of Alexei Mordashov (Severstal CEO, sanctioned by EU/UK/US/AU/JP/CA). SGCM invested in: Centice Corp (Series E, USD 9.86M, Mar 2013 + earlier debt round Jul 2012), FiberZone Networks (USD 12M round led by SGCM, Aug 2011), Advanced Diamond Technologies (Series D USD 5.2M led by SGCM, 2011; convertible note USD 0.84M, Dec 2013), Innolume (EUR 6M, 38% stake, 2008), Bisant (Series A USD 0.59M, Jun 2014), Competentum Group (via S-Group Ventures). Also managed S-Group Ventures (co-funded with Russian Venture Company) investing in Vocord (49% stake), Sonda Technologies (100% ownership). S-Group Direct Investments was a separate fund vehicle. SGCM is reportedly no longer investing.",
